N5008 [temp.variadic]/4-5 + [temp.deduct.call]/3.  A variadic constructor with a
FORWARDING-REFERENCE parameter pack `tuple(_U&&... __e) :
_Tuple_impl<0,_E...>(static_cast<_U&&>(__e)...)`, forwarding each element through
a recursive base, stores the correct element values for a heterogeneously-typed
pack (tuple<int,double>).  Previously the value pack `u` was replicated to
`u$k` but the parallel type pack `_U` in `static_cast<_U&&>` was left
unsubstituted, giving a static_cast type mismatch and an uninitialised member;
now the type pack's k-th element is substituted in lock-step.  This is the
forwarding-reference core of libstdc++ std::tuple's 3+-element constructor.
Non-vacuous: both element reads would be nondeterministic under the old collapse.
